# NIST SP 800-22 Statistical Test Suite Configuration

config COMPONENTS_NIST_SP800_22_ENABLE
    bool "Enable NIST SP 800-22 Statistical Test Suite"
    default n
    help
      Enable the NIST SP 800-22 Rev 1a statistical test suite for
      random number generator validation.

      This library implements all 15 tests:
      - 2.1  Frequency (Monobit) Test
      - 2.2  Frequency Test within a Block
      - 2.3  Runs Test
      - 2.4  Test for the Longest Run of Ones in a Block
      - 2.5  Binary Matrix Rank Test
      - 2.6  Discrete Fourier Transform (Spectral) Test
      - 2.7  Non-overlapping Template Matching Test
      - 2.8  Overlapping Template Matching Test
      - 2.9  Maurer's "Universal Statistical" Test
      - 2.10 Linear Complexity Test
      - 2.11 Serial Test
      - 2.12 Approximate Entropy Test
      - 2.13 Cumulative Sums Test
      - 2.14 Random Excursions Test
      - 2.15 Random Excursions Variant Test

      For full test suite execution, 1 million bits (~125KB) of random
      data is recommended. Some tests require this minimum for validity.

config NIST_KAT
    bool "Known-answer test against sts-2.1.2 reference (trng_kat)"
    default n
    depends on COMPONENTS_NIST_SP800_22_ENABLE
    help
      Embed a fixed 2^20-bit input (binary expansion of e, 128KB rodata)
      plus golden P-values generated by the official NIST sts-2.1.2
      reference implementation, and add the trng_kat shell command that
      runs the full suite on that input and compares every P-value.

      This validates the test implementation itself: a test whose
      decision statistic has silently degraded still passes statistical
      self-checks with good PRNG data, but cannot reproduce the
      reference P-values on fixed input.

      Regenerate the golden data with tools/gen_kat_golden.py.

config NIST_FULL_TEST
    bool "Enable full NIST SP 800-22 test suite"
    default n
    depends on COMPONENTS_NIST_SP800_22_ENABLE
    help
      Enable the complete NIST SP 800-22 test suite for official
      certification purposes.

      When enabled:
      - Non-overlapping Template: Tests all 148 official aperiodic
        templates (m=9) instead of 10 representative templates

      When disabled (default):
      - Non-overlapping Template uses 10 representative templates for
        faster execution; suitable for hardware tuning and development

      All other tests are identical in both modes (the Overlapping
      Template test always uses the exact NIST m=9 parameters).

      Enable this for final TRNG validation before submitting for
      NIST certification. The full test takes significantly longer.

config NIST_PRNG_VERIFY
    bool "Enable software PRNG verification commands"
    default n
    depends on COMPONENTS_NIST_SP800_22_ENABLE
    help
      Enable shell commands for verifying NIST test implementation
      using software PRNG (XORShift64*).

      Commands enabled:
      - trng_verify: Run NIST tests with software PRNG
      - trng_pattern: Debug pattern matching

      Use these commands to verify the test implementation is correct.
      If software PRNG passes but hardware TRNG fails, the issue is
      hardware quality, not implementation bugs.
